{"repositoryId":1257719180,"availability":"available","full":"monickverma/cursor-electronics","name":"cursor-electronics","description":"Circuit OS: AI hardware compiler. Plain English to validated schematic, Arduino firmware, SPICE simulation and BOM. Runs on AMD ROCm via vLLM.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-03T00:21:46Z","updated":"2026-10-17T11:54:55Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://circuit-os-ecru.vercel.app","topics":["ai","amd","arduino","electronics","hardware","kicad","llm","rocm","spice","vllm"],"demo":"https://circuit-os-ecru.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T19:17:17.863Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T19:17:17.863Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T19:17:17.863Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T11:46:10.260Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T19:17:17.863Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Describe a circuit in plain English → get a validated schematic, Arduino firmware, a SPICE simulation, a bill of materials, and an explanation of every design choice.","Live demo: circuit-os-ecru.vercel.app — runs in demo mode: five recorded designs (schematic, firmware, SPICE, BOM, validation) produced by the real deterministic pipeline via scripts/builddemofixtures.py. Free-text design needs the backend; see SETUP.md."],"features":["Hardware rule engine — floating nodes, voltage ratings, missing I²C pull-ups, RS-485 termination, PWM-capable pins","Simulation — ngspice runs in the background (Celery + Redis), graded pass/fail","Patching — \"make the LED brighter\" becomes a small patch that changes only what was asked","Explanations that focus on consequences — not \"R3 limits current\", but what breaks if you change R3","Runs on AMD — the same pipeline runs on an open model served by vLLM on ROCm, with a benchmark script"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/monickverma/curs